Subject: Wider view: more of the stadium on wide and tall screens (issue #91)
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

[display] wider_view is a host display setting outside the tweak mask. While
a match's stadium is drawn (GameRenderTask runs in its intros, play, pause and
replays only, and reports each frame), the host fills a window of another shape
than 16:9 with the picture and passes that shape against 16:9; the menus keep
the game's own 16:9 picture, as their screens are drawn for it. The 3D view
extends to the shape: more to the sides on a wider window, more above and below
on a taller one, everything the game's own view shows at its own size. The
HUD and the match's front-end overlays (centred layout), its 640 x 480 layer
(Mega Strike targets and pointer, score numbers), the scrolling text clip and
the picture in picture keep their 16:9 layout in the picture's middle; the
player markers and the Mega Strike meter follow the players across the whole
picture; full-screen layers (fades, bloom, depth of field, transitions) cover
it all, and the Mega Strike background keeps its shape, cropped.

Gameplay is unchanged: the AI's on-screen flags (IsInsideScreenMargin, sent to
every machine) use the game's own view, and the Mega Strike balls fly to the
targets where they show. At the shape 1 (the setting off, a 16:9 window, the
4:3 layout, the menus) every hook leaves the original values unchanged.

